  "2026-10-29T12:08:41.194Z",codex-agent,"Current-contract recovery proof is refreshed without reducing its mutant count: all nine deleted-identity, applied-result, fence, conversion, missing-base, ignore-routing, foreign-history, native-ID and minimum-host mutants fail 0/1; fixed source passes 8/8 (previously 7). Snapshot proof still detects both mutants and passes 2/2 fixed. Ownership acquisition, shared-writer selection and isolated custom-terminal permission probes retain all three failing mutants and pass 2/2 fixed. The old rollback-specific expectations are replaced by forward-only state transitions, while their native history and field-readback scenarios remain covered. All probes run in disposable copies; no production worktree mutation or weakened coverage threshold is used."
